# PawPi web app — environment variable example (NO real secrets here).
# Copy to `.env` and fill in real values. `.env` is gitignored; this file is committed.

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Payments foundation (Phase 2 ticket 2.3) — DO NOT COMMIT REAL KEYS.
#
# The payment layer reads these at runtime. If a rail's keys are UNSET, the payment
# routes return a clean "payments not configured" 503 and never crash — so the app runs
# fine without them until Tats sets up the accounts (sandbox first).
#
# Platform commission, in basis points (100 bps = 1%). Defaults to 0 when unset.
# PLATFORM_COMMISSION_BPS=500
#
# MercadoPago (fiat rail, primary — marketplace / split payments). Create a MercadoPago
# marketplace application (OAuth client) and register the redirect + webhook URLs.
# MP_CLIENT_ID=
# MP_CLIENT_SECRET=
# MP_WEBHOOK_SECRET=
# MP_REDIRECT_URI=https://<your-domain>/api/providers/<id>/payment-accounts/mercadopago/callback
#
# Binance Pay (crypto rail — merchant QR/deeplink + USDT settlement + Payout API).
# Create a Binance Pay merchant account and generate API key/secret.
# BINANCE_PAY_API_KEY=
# BINANCE_PAY_API_SECRET=
#
# Payment-token encryption-at-rest (Phase 2 ticket 2.16). A 32-byte symmetric key used to
# AES-256-GCM encrypt provider OAuth tokens (MercadoPago access/refresh) BEFORE they are
# stored. Accepts 64 hex chars OR base64 of 32 bytes. Generate one with, e.g.:
#   openssl rand -base64 32      (or:  openssl rand -hex 32)
# MUST be set BEFORE the first real provider connects a payment account (until then the
# connect flow returns a clean 503; existing plaintext rows still decrypt via passthrough).
# Keep it stable — rotating it makes previously-encrypted tokens unreadable. NEVER COMMIT A REAL VALUE.
# PAYMENTS_TOKEN_KEY=
#
# Shop auto-reorder scheduler (Phase 2 ticket 2.17). A shared secret guarding the
# machine-to-machine charge endpoint POST /api/payments/subscriptions/run. PawPi has NO
# built-in scheduler: wire an EXTERNAL one (host cron / scheduled job / CI cron) to POST that
# route daily with the header `x-cron-secret: <this value>`. If unset, the endpoint returns a
# clean 503 ("scheduler not configured") and never runs. NEVER COMMIT A REAL VALUE.
# CRON_SECRET=
#
# Telehealth video vendor (Phase 2 ticket 2.18) — DORMANT behind keys, exactly like payments.
# The consult-join route mints a room via a vendor-agnostic seam (apps/web/.../utils/video).
# If the keys are unset, joining a consult returns a clean 503 ("Video consults aren't set up
# yet") — consults still book + show the join button, nothing crashes. VIDEO_PROVIDER selects
# the adapter (default 'generic'); swap in a real Daily/Jitsi/Twilio adapter without touching
# the routes. NEVER COMMIT REAL VALUES.
# VIDEO_PROVIDER=generic
# VIDEO_API_KEY=
# VIDEO_API_SECRET=
# VIDEO_BASE_URL=https://<your-video-vendor-domain>
